==Trivia==
*The Omnitrix was originally called the Megawatt (alternatively spelled "Megawhat"), short for Megadeoxyribonucleictransdimensionaltransforminalnumerator.{{Refn|[[:File:Megawhat.PNG]]|group=DR}}{{Refn|https://archive.ph/rjEUR|group=JK}}{{Refn|[[:File:I10 Quick Facts OMNITRIX.png]]|group=pop-up}}{{Refn|''[[I-10: The Ben 10 User Generated Experience]]''|group=CN}}
*Originally, the Omnitrix only held thousands of DNA samples.{{Refn|group=pop-up|name=Omnitrix Merge DNA}}<ref name="ATTWT"/> This is retconned two ways:{{Refn|name=retcon|group=BTP}}
**Firstly, in ''[[War of the Worlds: Part 1]]'', it is revealed that the Omnitrix contained over one million DNA samples.
**Secondly, in ''[[Primus (Episode)|Primus]]'', the Omnitrix was revealed to be a wireless receiver for the [[Codon Stream]] instead of containing DNA.
*The Omnitrix's pre-reconfigured design was made by [[Dave Johnson]].{{Refn|[[:File:Dave Designed OS Ben, Gwen & Omnitrix.PNG]]|group=DJ}}
*The Omnitrix's reconfigured design was made by [[Norm Ryang]].{{Refn|[https://normart.blogspot.com/2010/09/omnitrix.html Norm's Ride - Omnitrix]|group = NR}}
*According to [[Dwayne McDuffie]], [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] could activate the Master Control via voice command, but he'd have to unlock it manually first.{{Refn|group=DM|name=link unavailable}}
*At the end of the episode ''[[War of the Worlds: Part 2]]'', it is heavily implied that the Omnitrix rebooted with an all-new roster of aliens, but this is completely ignored in the [[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 1|next episode]].{{Refn|group = BTP|name = retcon}} 
**Out-of-universe, this decision was made because of the toyline.{{Refn|https://archive.is/Xr98P|group = CM}}
**Ben found a couple unknown aliens while playing with the Omnitrix off-screen between ''[[War of the Worlds: Part 2]]'' and ''[[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 1]]''.{{Refn|group=DM|name=Archive2}}
*According to [[Derrick J. Wyatt]], [[Spitter]] was unlocked off-screen after '''''[[Ben 10: Destroy All Aliens]]''''' and is available to [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] in present day.{{Refn|group = DJW|name="Flashback aliens"}}
**However, according to [[Matt Wayne]], Ben had not unlocked Spitter as of ''[[The Frogs of War: Part 2]]''.{{Refn|[[:File:Spitter Not Unlocked in OV.png]]|group = MW}} It is unknown if he was unlocked afterwards.
*The Omnitrix is loaded with underpowered and powerless aliens that have not been seen on-screen, many of which had been unlocked when Ben was 11.{{Refn|[[:File:Underpowered Aliens Proof.png]]|group=MW}}
**Some joke aliens that [[Matt Wayne]] come up with that would fall under this category include [[Somnambulizard]], [[Bungee Sponge]], [[Skidmarx]], [[Mealymouth]], [[Hippopotamass]], and [[Crabtastic]].{{Refn|[[:File:Underpowered Joke Aliens Proof.png]]|group=MW}}
*The [[Galvan (Classic)|Galvans]] were the first species added to the Omnitrix.{{Refn|[[:File:Galvans First in the Omnitrix.png]]|group=DJW}} However, [[Grey Matter (Classic)|Grey Matter]]'s DNA sample came from neither Azmuth nor [[Albedo]].{{Refn|''link unavailable''|name=link unavailable|group=DJW}}
*The Omnitrix's green glow is its unique DNA energy signal.{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Green Glow.png]]|group=pop-up}}<ref name="Hunted">''[[Hunted]]''</ref>{{Refn|[[:File:Transformations happen instantly.png]]|group=pop-up}}{{Refn|group=DVD|name=XRBD}}
*Ben's transformations happen in an instant.{{Refn|[[:File:Vilgax's crew are robots.png]]|group=pop-up}}{{Refn|group=DVD|name=XRBD}} The series' [[Transformation Sequences]] show it in slow motion.{{Refn|[[:File:Slow Motion Transformations.png]]|group=pop-up}}<ref name="Hunted"/>
*Many of the problems Ben had with getting the Omnitrix to work were also safeguards put there by Azmuth.{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Safeguards.PNG]]|group=pop-up}}<ref name="SotO"/>
*Azmuth compared the Omnitrix to Noah's Ark and Ben to Noah.<ref name="WotW1"/>
*The Omnitrix's power source was smaller and more powerful than the [[Sub-Energy]].{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Power Source.png]]|group=pop-up}}{{Refn|group=DVD|name=XRBD}}
*Originally, the aliens' Omnitrix symbols' grey and white coloration in the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''' was caused by a malfunction.{{Refn|[[:File:OS Grey and White Symbols Original Explanation.PNG]]|group=DM}} In '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', the cause of the coloration was changed to a scratch guard that Ben didn't know how to remove. It fell off after '''''[[Ben 10: Destroy All Aliens]]'''''.{{Refn|group=DJW|name=scratch}}
**From a design standpoint, the Omnitrix symbols were mostly changed because that's how the crew decided to color it for 10-year-old Ben's appearance in '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]'''.{{Refn|[[:File:UA Young Ben Green Omnitrix Symbol.PNG]]|group=DM|name=Clothes}}
**During the early development of '''Omniverse''', it was decided from the get-go that 11-year-old Ben's aliens would all have green Omnitrix symbols.{{Refn|[[:File:OV Young Ben Omnitrix Symbol Color.png]]|group=DJW}}
**However, it is open to interpretation whether the Omnitrix's grey and white symbol no longer exists or is just another shade of green and black due to a change in art style, as in ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', as soon as [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Prime]] receives the Omnitrix for the first time and turns into [[Heatblast (Classic)|Heatblast]], his Omnitrix symbol is black and green instead of grey and white.
*Most of the Omnitrix aliens wore outfits similar to 10/11-year-old Ben's black and white T-shirt in the '''Original Series''' and '''Omniverse''' flashbacks was because they looked cool and helped make all the aliens appear with a common thread.{{Refn|[[:File:OS Aliens Clothing Explanation.png]]|group=DJ}} These clothes also helped tie the aliens to Ben, even if they were unable to work with certain aliens.{{Refn|[[:File:OS Aliens Clothing Explanation 2.PNG]]|group=DJ}}
**This feature was removed when the Omnitrix reconfigured. When asked if he would give Ben's aliens Ben's clothing, [[Dwayne McDuffie]] replied "Likely never."{{Refn|group=DM|name=Clothes}}
*According to Derrick, the reconfigured Omnitrix had technical glitches that would cause random flight and abilities not native to the alien species.{{Refn|group=DJW|name=glitches}}
**However, it is unknown if this is canon as Matt seemed to be unaware of the existence of glitch powers.{{Refn|http://archive.is/A42xJ|group=MW}}
*Besides being the intergalactic peace symbol,{{Refn|name=PeaceInOurTime|group=DM}} the Omnitrix's hourglass symbol serves as the insignia for the [[Galvan (Classic)|Galvan]]'s technology.{{Refn|[[:File:Galvan Tech Symbol Proof.PNG]]|group=DJW}} 
**In '''Alien Force''' and '''Ultimate Alien''', this symbol was seen on the [[Plumbers (Classic)|Plumbers]] [[Plumber Badge|badges]].
*In ''[[Max Out]]'', the reconfigured Omnitrix spoke in a voice similar to Ben's, but deeper. In all following episodes, it spoke in Ben's normal voice.
*The Omnitrix's voice-activated self-destruct sequence is the same code from '''''Star Trek III: The Search for Spock''''' that James T. Kirk used to activate the Enterprise's one minute self-destruct sequence (000 destruct-0).
*The reconfigured Omnitrix aliens yelled their names after Ben transformed into them because "they were asserting their identity as they gained consciousness".{{Refn|group=DM|name=shouting}}
**According to [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]], he shouted the aliens' names to insert fear into his enemies.<ref name="PN775IM">''[[Prisoner Number 775 is Missing]]''</ref>
**It was [[Dwayne McDuffie]]'s idea to have Ben shout the names of his aliens, as he thought it would help younger fans know the aliens' names.{{Refn|[[:File:Ben Shouting Out Alien Names.PNG]]|group=DM}}
**Ben would later stop doing this prior to '''Omniverse''' because "he got tired of it".{{Refn|[[:File:Ben Got Tired of Shouting His Aliens' Names.png]]|group=MW}}
*Ben set several layers of security to the reconfigured Omnitrix, coded to his DNA and voice, to make tampering more difficult. This is one of the reasons Vilgax was unable to manipulate the Omnitrix like he did in the '''Original Series'''.{{Refn|group=DM|name=bonded}}
*One of the sounds used for the reconfigured Omnitrix is called "Computer, beeps 11".{{Refn|group=AM|https://www.audiomicro.com/little-tinkly-beeps-computer-beep-royalty-free-stock-music-972024}}
*[[Duncan Rouleau]] believes that the alien DNA is "injected" into the user, meaning they retain the wielder's personality, memories, and consciousness.{{Refn|[[:File:Alien DNA Injected.PNG]]|group=DR}} Because of this, most of the aliens are not full-blown aliens, with the exceptions of [[Ectonurite (Classic)|Ectonurite]] and [[Conductoid]] DNA.{{Refn|[[:File:Most Aliens Aren't Full Aliens.png]]|group=DR}}
*The Omnitrix could not transform the user into another of their own species.
*Duncan Rouleau believes that this Omnitrix had the [[Omni-Kix Armors]] locked off-screen.{{Refn|[[:File:Omni-Kix in Classic.png]]|group=DR}}
*A common error in the first episodes of the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''' is that in some scenes the Omnitrix featured an extra activation button on the right side.
**This error is also present in '''''[[Ben 10: Destroy All Aliens]]''''' and all throughout the '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''' flashbacks.
*The Omnitrix has protection against [[Nanite (Generator Rex)|Nanites]].{{Refn|[[:File:The Omnitrix has protection against Nanites.png]]|group=DR}}
*To promote [[Ben 10: Alien Swarm]] premiere, a contest was held in which the winner would receive an Omnitrix sweepstakes watch.
